Let $X$ be a smooth projective K3 surface defined over $\mathbb{R}$, with complex points $X(\mathbb{C})$ and real locus $X(\mathbb{R})$, and let $f : X \to X$ be an automorphism defined over $\mathbb{R}$. Denote by $\lambda_1(f)$ the dynamical degree of $f$, i.e. the spectral radius of $f^*$ acting on $H^{1,1}(X(\mathbb{C}),\mathbb{R})$, and by $h_{\mathrm{top}}(f, Y)$ the topological entropy of $f$ restricted to an $f$-invariant subset $Y$. Recall that $h_{\mathrm{top}}(f, X(\mathbb{C})) = \log \lambda_1(f)$ by Gromov–Yomdin, and that the Fatou set of $f$ on $X(\mathbb{C})$ is the largest open subset where the family $\{f^n\}_{n \geq 0}$ is locally equicontinuous.

Does there exist such a pair $(X, f)$ with $\lambda_1(f) > 1$, with $X(\mathbb{R}) \neq \emptyset$, and satisfying at least one of the following three properties?
\begin{enumerate}
\item $h_{\mathrm{top}}(f, X(\mathbb{R})) = h_{\mathrm{top}}(f, X(\mathbb{C}))$;
\item there is a connected component $S$ of $X(\mathbb{R})$ with $h_{\mathrm{top}}(f|_S, S) = 0$;
\item some connected component $S$ of $X(\mathbb{R})$ is entirely contained in the Fatou set of $f$ on $X(\mathbb{C})$.
\end{enumerate>

